"""Hand-written data for the artist pages (/artists/ and /artists/<slug>), built by build_pages.py.

Targets "[artist] paintings" searches and, for the index, "famous artists" (Ahrefs US, Nov 2026:
109K/mo, KD 2) and "famous painters" (17K, KD 13). Examples: monet paintings 34K KD 8,
van gogh paintings 47K KD 29, hokusai 19K KD 29, caravaggio paintings 13K KD 2,
goya paintings 10K KD 1.

Lives, dates and where-to-see lines are written here and kept to settled facts. A work appears on
an artist's page only if its record came from the holding museum's own open-access data (met, aic,
nga, cleveland, smithsonian, smk), from the curated wiki- set, or is a hand-checked entry in
famous_paintings.py or EXTRA below. The catalog's other Wikimedia records are left out because
their museums, media and sometimes images are wrong. Every wiki- and EXTRA image was checked by eye.
"""

# Fields:
#   slug, name, short (for "by Monet"), pron ("his"/"her"), names (catalog artist names)
#   born, died (display); birth, death (ISO or year, for structured data)
#   nationality, movements (art-movements anchors), known (titles), group (index section)
#   lede, life (paragraphs), see (where to see), faq [(q, a)], wp (wallpaper page slug)
#   must: catalog ids always shown (the best-known works), in priority order
#   works_word: "paintings" or "prints"; max_year: leave out later works (copyright)
#   titles: {id: English title} where the museum's own title isn't English
#   exclude: catalog ids to leave out (near-duplicates in a series)
